# Deterministic firing scenario for reproducible stills.
#
# The game's primary trigger is the LEFT MOUSE BUTTON, and that is what this
# script drives: `--input-script` takes `<frame> Mouse.Left <down|up>` as well
# as key names. (The `Mouse.` prefix is required — a bare `Left` is the ARROW
# KEY.) A scripted press feeds both the `mouseButton` rising edge and the held
# `snapshot.mouse.buttons.left` level state, which is what makes the weapon
# full-auto — the same two paths a real click drives.
#
#   functor -d examples/shooting-range run native \
#     --input-script firing.input --script-dt 0.016 \
#     --capture-frame .captures/firing.png --capture-at-frame 36
#
# The trigger is held from frame 0. The weapon is full-auto at one round per
# `fireInterval` (0.18 s) = 12 frames at --script-dt 0.016, so shots leave the
# barrel on frames 0, 12, 24, 36, ... Capturing exactly on a shot frame catches
# the muzzle flash (flashLife 0.055 s ~ 3 frames) and the tracer (tracerLife
# 0.075 s ~ 4 frames) while they are at full brightness, with several rounds of
# recoil already accumulated in the crosshair spread.
0 Mouse.Left down
